%% Owner-driven subagent review — what the subagent_review phase actually does:
%% the owner fans out to fresh, independent subagents (one per material-driven
%% lens, NOT forks of its own context), runs them in parallel, and synthesizes
%% their findings into the closing summary.
%%
%% This diagram is scoped to the subagent dynamics, which are identical whichever
%% door the phase was entered through. The engine-side TRIGGERS that get here —
%% critic death or silence (3s debounce, auto-resume up to 5, grace timer,
%% canFallbackOnDeath), and the direct `review +subagent` request — are in
%% flow-protocol-robustness.mmd. enterFallbackPhase / enterDirectSubagentPhase in
%% protocol-runner.ts are the seam between the two.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant PR as protocol-runner.ts
    participant Owner as Owner session
    participant LA as subagent lens A
    participant LB as subagent lens B
    participant LN as subagent lens N

    Note over PR: THREE doors into one phase.<br/>death — critic exited, auto-resume exhausted<br/>silence — critic alive, but its window elapsed with nothing posted<br/>direct — review +subagent, no critic ever spawned
    PR->>PR: fire the `fallback` transition into subagent_review,<br/>then retire the critic — death and silence both have one,<br/>direct has nobody to retire
    PR->>Owner: onFallback instructions via transport<br/>(a thread post alone would not wake it)<br/>each door passes its own FallbackContext arm, so the preamble<br/>can only state facts that door actually had

    Note over Owner: pick the lenses the MATERIAL calls for.<br/>code → correctness, layering, tests.<br/>design doc → assumptions, alternatives, failure modes

    par one FRESH subagent per chosen lens (independent, not forks)
        Owner->>LA: spawn: "re-read this thread + the diff/spec,<br/>orient yourself, review for lens A"
        LA->>LA: orient from source, review
        LA-->>Owner: findings (lens A)
    and
        Owner->>LB: spawn: review for lens B
        LB->>LB: orient from source, review
        LB-->>Owner: findings (lens B)
    and
        Owner->>LN: spawn: review for lens N
        LN->>LN: orient from source, review
        LN-->>Owner: findings (lens N)
    end

    Note over Owner: synthesize — resolve conflicts across lenses,<br/>drop the noise, keep what is real
    Owner->>PR: advance({ content: summary })
    Note over PR: summary_posted → complete<br/>summary → CompletionEvent.summary (factory PM reads it)<br/>via: 'fallback' | 'direct' + degradation → the PM line says it was owner-run
